  "autoMode": {
    "soft_deny": [
      "$defaults",
      "Bash(mix ecto.drop:*) — Sensitive Remote Exec / Irreversible Local Destruction carve-out reinforcement for non-local DB targets in sanbase2",
      "Bash(psql:*) and Bash(pg_dump:*) against non-localhost DATABASE_URL in this repo",
      "Bash(prodkubectl:*) — shell history shows frequent (8x) use of what appears to be a prod-scoped kubectl wrapper; propose as soft-deny carve-out pending confirmation of intent per prod-namespace write caution",
      "Bash(remote_console:*) and Bash(premote_console:*) — shell history shows frequent (22x combined) use of remote console tools, which may reach non-local systems; propose as soft-deny consistent with Remote Shell Writes / Sensitive Remote Exec defaults"
    ],
    "environment": [
      "### Org-wide",
      "**Organization**: Santiment (github.com/santiment — inferred from repo remote `santiment/sanbase2`)",
      "**Repository visibility**: Public (github santiment/sanbase2, confirmed via gh)",
      "**Internal sharing / snippet hosting**: None configured — treat public paste/gist services as outside the trust boundary",
      "**Default / protected branches**: Default branch `master`; protected branches: `master` (via gh); Rulesets: none listed",
      "**Network posture**: WireGuard VPN required to reach stage/production services (e.g. *.stage.san resolves only over VPN, per .env.example)",
      "**Source control**: the git repository the session started in (usually under ~/work or ~/code) and its own remotes; main repo is santiment/sanbase2 (public)",
      "**Sensitive data locations & audiences**: .env.dev, .env.example, config/prod.exs, config/*.secret.exs, load_test/data/apikeys.json, lib/sanbase/disagreement_tweets/tweet_classification.ex — any credentials, personal data, or regulated data in these; share only with audiences cleared at the [named+specifics] bar",
      "**Sensitive remote targets**: any namespace, host, or container whose name carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment (hyphen/underscore/dot-delimited — e.g. matches `prod-db`, not `producer`)",
      "**Protected IaC scopes**: IAM, RBAC, networking, quota, and node-pool resources; anything whose name or tag carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment",
      "### User-specific",
      "**Primary use of Claude Code**: software development (Elixir/Phoenix GraphQL API — sanbase2)",
      "**Trusted repos**: the git repository the session started in, under ~/work or ~/code; main one santiment/sanbase2 (github.com:santiment/sanbase2.git, public — confidential material never goes into it)",
      "**Org-specific CLIs**: kubectl, prodkubectl, remote_console, premote_console may reach stage/prod — treat as sensitive remote exec; ~/.claude/bin/ch-prod-ro is the only sanctioned prod access (read-only ClickHouse)",
      "Git commits/pushes: never commit or push without explicit per-request instruction from the user (per ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md); this applies only to that one request and never carries over"
    ]
  }
